 200 countries and territories, it holds a leading share in global savory snacks and ranks as the second-largest beverage provider worldwide behind Coca-Cola, with exposure to carbonated soft drinks (CSD), water, sports, and energy drinks. Convenience foods accounted for approximately 58% of total 2025 net revenue, with beverages comprising the remainder. PepsiCo owns most of its US manufacturing and distribution capacity, while relying on bottlers internationally. International markets represented 41% of sales and 46% of operating profit before corporate expenses in 2025.</p><button class=\"linkish\" type=\"button\" data-more>More</button></div><dl class=fields><dt>Industry</dt><dd><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"industry:beverages\">Beverages</a></dd><dt>Country</dt><dd><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"country:US\">United States</a></dd></dl><h3 class=\"sub\">Betas</h3><table class=\"cmp \"><thead><tr><th></th><th class=\"n\">Beta</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:1\">S&amp;P 500</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">0.07</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:2\">Long Treasury yield</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">0.28</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:3\">US dollar against major currencies</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">−0.26</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:4\">Crude oil price</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">0.00</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:5\">Semiconductor stocks</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">−0.37</span></td></tr><tr><th><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:6\">Bitcoin</a></th><td class=n><span class=\"n v\">−0.06</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 class=\"sub\">Events</h3><table class=\"ifs\"><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>If Yes</th><th>If No</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-k=\"ev:prop:4\"><td><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"prop:4\">China blockades or attacks Taiwan by May 18, 2027</a><div